# Functype Library Developer – NonEmptyArray Implementation Guide

## Overview

Guide for adding a `NonEmptyArray` type to the functype library. This type guarantees at least one element and implements key functional interfaces. Follow these patterns to integrate it into the codebase.

## Prerequisites

- **Node.js**: ≥ 18.0.0  
- **pnpm**: 10.12.1  
- **TypeScript**: Strict mode enabled  

## Core Implementation

### NonEmptyArray – Basic Structure

Unlike other containers, NonEmptyArray uses a **class-based** approach for simplicity and readability.

```typescript
// src/nonEmptyArray/index.ts
import { Base } from "@/core/base"

export class NonEmptyArray<T> {
  private readonly values: T[]

  constructor(...values: T[]) {
    if (values.length === 0) {
      throw new Error("NonEmptyArray requires at least one element")
    }
    this.values = values
  }

  // Functor – map
  map<B>(f: (value: T) => B): NonEmptyArray<B> {
    return new NonEmptyArray(...this.values.map(f))
  }

  // Monad – flatMap (not Monad interface, just a method)
  flatMap<B>(f: (value: T) => NonEmptyArray<B>): NonEmptyArray<B> {
    // Simple flattening of nested arrays
    const result: B[] = []
    for (const v of this.values) {
      const inner = f(v)
      result.push(...inner.toArray())
    }
    return new NonEmptyArray(...result)
  }

  // Foldable – fold (basic version)
  fold<B>(f: (value: T) => B): B {
    return f(this.values[0]) // only first element!
  }

  // head / tail
  head(): T {
    return this.values[0]
  }

  tail(): NonEmptyArray<T> | undefined {
    if (this.values.length === 1) return undefined
    return new NonEmptyArray(...this.values.slice(1))
  }

  // toArray
  toArray(): T[] {
    return [...this.values]
  }
}
```

### Companion Functions

```typescript
export function NonEmptyArrayOf<T>(...values: T[]): NonEmptyArray<T> {
  return new NonEmptyArray<T>(...values)
}

export function fromArray<T>(arr: T[]): NonEmptyArray<T> | undefined {
  if (arr.length === 0) return undefined
  return new NonEmptyArray<T>(...arr)
}

// Attach to constructor
NonEmptyArray.of = NonEmptyArrayOf
NonEmptyArray.fromArray = fromArray
```

> ⚠️ **Important**: The class does **not** implement the `Monad` interface from functype, only the `flatMap` method is provided. `fold` only operates on the head element, which is **not** the standard `Foldable` contract. These simplifications are intentional for initial development.

